<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN SHAREHOLDER OKAYS GOSHAWK BID FOR MATHESON.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN SHAREHOLDER OKAYS GOSHAWK BID FOR MATHESON.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian holding company Monceau-Zolder said on Friday its Brederode Insurance unit had responded favourably to the takeover bid by Goshawk Insurance Holdings Plc for Matheson's Lloyd's Investment Trust Plc (MLIT) in which Brederode Insurance holds about 30 precent.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the takeover price for the MLIT stake was 71.24 percent payable in cash with the remainder in new shares, issued by Goshawk and quoted on the Alternative Investment Market of the London bourse.</p>
<p>Monceau-Zolder, part of the Brederode group, said Brederode Insurance had made an important capital gain which would be included second half accounts.</p>
<p>It said Brederode Insurance had acquired 3.77 percent of Goshawk's capital through the operation.</p>
<p>-- Bert Lauwers, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
